---
import Container from '../components/ui/Container.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/ui/SectionHeading.astro';
import { mailto, site } from '../data/site';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | Joyful Minds Counselling';
const description =
  'How Joyful Minds Counselling handles website enquiries, call-back requests, email delivery through Resend and planned Google Analytics use.';
const policyLinkClass = 'rounded-sm text-terracotta underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-terracotta-hover';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} breadcrumbLabel="Privacy Policy">
  <section aria-labelledby="privacy-title" class="bg-canvas py-16 sm:py-20 lg:py-24">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionHeading id="privacy-title" title="Privacy Policy" headingLevel="h1" eyebrow="Joyful Minds Counselling">
        <p>Your privacy matters, especially when you are considering counselling.</p>
      </SectionHeading>
      <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-11-16">November 16, 2026</time></p>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink">
        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-scope" class="space-y-4">
          <h2 id="privacy-scope" class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-forest sm:text-3xl">1. About this policy</h2>
          <p>
            This policy explains how {site.name}, operated by {site.practitioner}, handles personal information
            collected through this website and related enquiries. It covers browsing, contacting Rhonda and requesting
            a call-back.
          </p>
          <p>
            This website is not a clinical record system. Consent to counselling, clinical confidentiality, recordkeeping
            and the limits of confidentiality are addressed separately as part of arranging counselling. This policy does
            not limit your rights under applicable privacy law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-collection" class="space-y-4">
          <h2 id="privacy-collection" class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-forest sm:text-3xl">2. Information you provide</h2>
          <p>The request-a-call-back form collects:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
            <li>Your name and phone number.</li>
            <li>Your province of residence, Alberta or Ontario.</li>
            <li>Your preferred time to receive a call, if you choose to provide it.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            The form does not ask for an email address or clinical information. Please include only scheduling details,
            including your time zone, and do not enter diagnoses, symptoms, treatment history or other private health
            information. If you contact Rhonda directly by email or phone, you choose what information to share; an email
            also includes your email address and any message or attachments you send.
          </p>
          <p>
            Website forms and ordinary email are not suitable for emergencies or confidential clinical discussions.
            No internet or email service can guarantee complete security. If you prefer not to use the form or email,
            you can call <a href={site.phoneHref} class={policyLinkClass}>{site.phone}</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-use" class="space-y-4">
          <h2 id="privacy-use" class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-forest sm:text-3xl">3. How information is used</h2>
          <p>
            Information you provide is used to respond to your enquiry, arrange a call or consultation, confirm the
            province in which you are seeking services, and manage related communications. Technical information may
            also be used to operate the website, investigate delivery problems and protect against misuse.
          </p>
          <p>
            Submitting a request authorizes Rhonda to use its details to respond to you. It does not sign you up for
            marketing or provide consent to optional analytics. We do not sell your personal information or use
            website enquiries for targeted advertising.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-providers" class="space-y-4">
          <h2 id="privacy-providers" class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-forest sm:text-3xl">4. Website and communication providers</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>Resend:</strong> The website uses Resend to deliver call-back requests to Rhonda by email.
            Your submitted name, phone number, province and optional callback time are included in that email.
            Resend processes the message and delivery-related information to provide its email service. The delivered
            message is also handled by the receiving email provider. See
            {' '}<a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" class={policyLinkClass}>Resend's privacy policy</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Vercel:</strong> The website is hosted on Vercel. Hosting infrastructure may process technical
            information such as IP addresses, requested URLs, browser or device details, request times and diagnostic
            logs to deliver and secure the website. See
            {' '}<a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-notice" class={policyLinkClass}>Vercel's privacy notice</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Google Tag Manager:</strong> When configured on the production website, Google Tag Manager
            loads resources from Google to manage website tags. These requests may disclose technical information
            such as your IP address and browser details to Google. Tag Manager does not by itself mean Google
            Analytics is enabled; our planned analytics use is explained below. Tags and any required consent
            controls must be configured before optional tracking is activated.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Jane:</strong> Appointment links take you to the practice's booking site on Jane.
            Information you enter there is handled within that separate service, not by this website's call-back form.
            Review the privacy information presented by Jane before submitting booking or health information.
          </p>
          <p>
            Service providers may process or store information outside your province or Canada, including in the
            United States. Information may be subject to the laws of those jurisdictions and lawful access by their
            authorities. Provider policies describe their own practices; please contact Rhonda with questions about
            the handling of your enquiry.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-analytics" class="space-y-4">
          <h2 id="privacy-analytics" class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-forest sm:text-3xl">5. Cookies and planned Google Analytics use</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>Google Analytics is planned but is not currently enabled on this website.</strong>
            We plan to use it to understand website traffic and improve the site's content and usability, not to
            assess an individual's mental health or make decisions about counselling.
          </p>
          <p>
            When enabled, Google Analytics may use cookies and similar identifiers to collect information about pages
            viewed, website interactions, referral sources, browser and device characteristics, and approximate
            location. Visiting a counselling-related page can itself reveal sensitive interests; analytics information
            should not be assumed to be anonymous.
          </p>
          <p>
            We will not intentionally send names, phone numbers, email addresses, form contents or counselling
            information to Google Analytics. Before activation, we will review the configuration and applicable consent
            requirements, provide any required notices and choices, and update this policy to describe the actual
            implementation. Publishing this policy alone does not activate analytics or obtain consent.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can manage or delete cookies through your browser. Google also provides an
            {' '}<a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout/" class={policyLinkClass}>Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>
            {' '}for supported browsers. These browser tools do not replace any consent choices the website may be
            required to provide. Learn more in
            {' '}<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class={policyLinkClass}>Google's privacy policy</a>
            {' '}and its
            {' '}<a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6004245" class={policyLinkClass}>Analytics data safeguards information</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-sharing" class="space-y-4">
          <h2 id="privacy-sharing" class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-forest sm:text-3xl">6. Other disclosures</h2>
          <p>
            Information may be shared with providers as needed to operate the website and respond to you, with your
            consent, or where disclosure is required or permitted by applicable law, including a valid legal requirement
            or a serious safety concern. Clinical confidentiality and its limits are discussed separately before
            counselling.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-retention" class="space-y-4">
          <h2 id="privacy-retention" class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-forest sm:text-3xl">7. Retention and safeguards</h2>
          <p>
            Enquiry information is retained for as long as reasonably needed to respond, manage related communications
            and meet applicable legal or professional obligations. Emails, delivery records, logs and backups may have
            different retention periods depending on the provider and account settings. This policy does not promise
            immediate deletion from every provider or backup.
          </p>
          <p>
            We use reasonable safeguards appropriate to the information involved, but no method of transmission or
            storage is completely secure. Please keep website requests limited to scheduling details. Clinical records,
            if a counselling relationship begins, are subject to separate professional recordkeeping requirements.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-choices" class="space-y-4">
          <h2 id="privacy-choices" class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-forest sm:text-3xl">8. Your choices and privacy questions</h2>
          <p>
            You can choose not to submit information through the website. You may contact Rhonda to ask about
            information held about you, request access or correction, ask about retention or deletion, withdraw consent
            to optional uses, or raise a privacy concern. Requests are handled subject to applicable law and any
            professional retention obligations. Identity verification may be needed to protect your information.
            Withdrawing permission to use your contact details may mean Rhonda cannot respond to your request.
          </p>
          <p>
            For privacy enquiries, contact {site.practitioner} at
            {' '}<a href={mailto('Privacy enquiry')} class:list={[policyLinkClass, 'break-all']}>{site.email}</a>
            {' '}or <a href={site.phoneHref} class={policyLinkClass}>{site.phone}</a>.
            Please do not include sensitive clinical details in an initial email. You may also raise concerns with the
            privacy regulator that has jurisdiction over your information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-changes" class="space-y-4">
          <h2 id="privacy-changes" class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-forest sm:text-3xl">9. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            This policy may be updated when website features, providers or privacy practices change. The date above
            identifies the latest revision. Any additional notice or consent required for a material change will be
            provided as applicable.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>
</Layout>
